# Domain Logic

## Chemistry (`src/lib/chemistry/`)

Pure functions for pool/spa water science — no React imports in core modules.

- `status.ts`, `ranges.ts` — evaluate readings against profile targets
- `test-recommendations.ts`, `dosing-tips.ts` — actionable advice
- `tip-to-maintenance.ts` — bridge tips → maintenance task inputs
- `use-recommendation-maintenance.ts` — hook only when React state is needed

Keep saltwater, CYA, free chlorine, pH, alkalinity logic here, not in components.

## Validations (`src/lib/validations/`)

One Zod schema per form entity:

```ts
export const waterTestSchema = z.object({ /* fields */ });
export type WaterTestFormValues = z.infer<typeof waterTestSchema>;
```

- String fields for numeric inputs that may be empty (parse in submit handler)
- Import schemas in form components via `@hookform/resolvers/zod`

## Setup (`src/lib/setup/`)

Onboarding data only — defaults, equipment presets, types. UI lives in `src/components/setup/`.

## When adding chemistry features

1. Add pure logic in `src/lib/chemistry/`
2. Add Zod schema if a new form is involved
3. Surface results in feature components via imports from `lib/`, not inline calculations
